description: Strict TypeScript standard for the project
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# TypeScript

- Strict mode always on. No `any` – use `unknown` plus narrowing.
- `type` for props, return types, and unions. `interface` only for extensible public APIs.
- Explicit return types on exported functions and hooks.
- Prefer `readonly` for immutable props/arrays.
- Prefer `satisfies` over type assertions when possible.
- Avoid non-null assertions (`!`). Narrow instead.
